CORE
sufficient.c
--enforce-contract f _ --pointer-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[f\.precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.
--
A sufficient legacy function contract establishes the generated static-array
precondition before the implementation runs. The harness call to the marked
contract-checking wrapper receives no static-array precondition, so the check
happens only after the requires clauses have been assumed.
